[
  {
    "id": "I01",
    "text": "Hi! Let's count prime numbers."
  },
  {
    "id": "I02",
    "text": "A prime number is a whole number greater than one with exactly two positive factors: one and itself."
  },
  {
    "id": "I03",
    "text": "A factor divides a number evenly, with nothing left over."
  },
  {
    "id": "I04",
    "text": "Let's try five tiles."
  },
  {
    "id": "I05",
    "text": "Five makes one row of five. Its only factors are one and five."
  },
  {
    "id": "I06",
    "text": "Six also makes two rows of three. Six has more than two factors, so it is not prime."
  },
  {
    "id": "I07",
    "text": "Turning a rectangle around does not give us new factors."
  },
  {
    "id": "I08",
    "text": "One has only one factor: one. So one is not prime."
  },
  {
    "id": "I09",
    "text": "Now let's count every prime number below one thousand."
  },
  {
    "id": "T002a",
    "text": "Two has exactly two factors: one and two."
  },
  {
    "id": "T002b",
    "text": "Any larger even number has two as another factor."
  },
  {
    "id": "T002c",
    "text": "Two is the only even prime."
  },
  {
    "id": "T009a",
    "text": "Nine is odd, but three rows of three make nine."
  },
  {
    "id": "T009b",
    "text": "Nine has factors other than one and itself. It is not prime."
  },
  {
    "id": "T101a",
    "text": "Ninety-eight, ninety-nine, and one hundred have extra factors."
  },
  {
    "id": "T101b",
    "text": "The next prime after ninety-seven is one hundred one."
  },
